  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Scannable
  displayName: Hallucigenia
  scientificName: Tripneustes Hallucigenia
  description: Good heavens! The creature is a pale blue worm of considerable length,
    furnished along its dorsal ridge with paired spines of a most aggressively symmetrical
    arrangement. It moves with a calm, unhurried purpose that is altogether more
    unnerving than if it were to scuttle. The taxonomists who named this genus were,
    I think, being rather honest about the experience of encountering one.
  journalImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 144ff0253bf21d34cb46be022b944373, type: 3}
